## Technologies Used in WikiGraph

| Technology              | Purpose                                                                              |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| HTML5                   | Structures the webpage and dashboard components.                                     |
| CSS3                    | Provides custom styling, animations, and visual effects.                             |
| JavaScript              | Handles search functionality, API requests, graph generation, and user interactions. |
| Tailwind CSS            | Creates responsive layouts and modern UI styling.                                    |
| Vis Network             | Visualizes topics and their relationships through an interactive graph.              |
| Wikipedia MediaWiki API | Fetches article summaries and related links.                                         |
| Font Awesome 6.4.0      | Provides icons for navigation and controls.                                          |
| Google Fonts (Inter)    | Improves typography and readability.                                                 |
| Browser LocalStorage    | Saves search history and bookmarked topics locally.                                  |
| Fetch API               | Retrieves information from Wikipedia.                                                |
| Netlify                 | Hosts and deploys the website.                                                       |

### Technology categories

- Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Tailwind CSS
- Graph visualization: Vis Network
- External API: Wikipedia MediaWiki API
- Browser storage: LocalStorage
- Icons and fonts: Font Awesome, Google Fonts
- Deployment: Netlify

Important: The supplied source code confirms the frontend libraries and Wikipedia API. Netlify is the website's hosting platform based on the provided URL. The project does not currently use a dedicated backend, database, or AI/ML model.
